{"Whitelist bypass via unanchored regex - the regex `@(#{domains})` matches the whitelisted domain as a substring, so `user@vaynermedia.com.evil.com` passes a whitelist of `vaynermedia.com` because `@vaynermedia.com` appears as a substring. An attacker can register any domain like `vaynermedia.com.attacker.com` to bypass the whitelist. The regex should be anchored to the end of the string with `\\z`": 0.906444787979126}